/-!
# The original cocode series and centered transvections in L_z

The native perfect sextet residual generates the whole cocode by
commutators. Transport to the original action and relative normality give
[V,L_z]=V and V≤O₂(L_z). The original two-core maps onto all 64 native
translations, with kernel exactly V. The literal V_z=[V,O₂(L_z)] is the
seven-dimensional pair space, its next commutator is the original line
⟨z⟩, and both inclusions ⟨z⟩<V_z<V are strict. The original L_z T normalizes
this series. The two-core action on V_z has kernel V and common fixed group
⟨z⟩, using the full native group of centered transvections.

The earlier cocode marking remains an input; no residual containment,
translation coverage, commutator-space or fixed-line callback is assumed.
The original quotient L_z/O₂(L_z) remains the nonsplit 3.A₆ with its cubic
center. These results discharge the containment and transvection inputs of
8.2.11 and the fixed-line input of 8.2.12. The residual module-factor
identifications, normal-closure geometry, remaining Mathieu branches and
ambient J4 recognition remain with qt-d-1222-nonff-mathieu.
Source: Aschbacher–Smith H.15.3, 8.2.11–12, printed pp.400,722,
refs/quasithin.pdf. The imported native model retains its ATLAS attribution.
-/

public noncomputable section
